<h1>PROM End-Term Numericals Workbook</h1>
<p class="lede">A study guide that teaches you each chapter first (what is in it, the formulas, the reasoning), then walks you through every numerical question step by step.</p>

<h3 style="margin-top:28px">How to use this file</h3>
<ol class="steps"><li><b>Read the chapter overview and concepts first.</b> They give you the vocabulary. Numbers make sense only after that.</li><li><b>Read the formulas section.</b> Each formula has a 'why it works' box; if you understand the reason, you will not forget the formula.</li><li><b>Open the book or slides at the page shown</b> in each question card (e.g. 'Book Ch 2, Exercise 4 · p. 68'). Try the question on paper.</li><li><b>Click 'Show the solution and the teaching'.</b> The first question of every type is taught slowly. Later ones of the same type show the answer and what is different.</li><li><b>Tick 'I have practiced this'</b> when you can do it without looking. The sidebar counts your progress (it is saved in your browser).</li><li><b>Finish with the one-page summary</b> at the end of each chapter. Use the print button at the top for a PDF.</li></ol>

<h3>The exam, and what this workbook covers</h3>
