<h4>Omega vs Alpha at 18%</h4>
<div class="restate"><p>You work for the 3T company, which expects to earn at least 18 percent on investments. You have to choose between two similar projects. The chart shows the cash information for each project (Years Y0 to Y7, inflow, outflow and net flow). Which of the two projects would you fund if the decision were based only on financial information? Why?</p>
<p class="mini"><b>Net flows.</b> Omega: −225,000; −190,000; 150,000; 190,000; 215,000; 175,000; 197,000; 70,000 (total 582,000). Alpha: −300,000; −50,000; 150,000; 200,000; 250,000; 150,000; 180,000; 90,000 (total 670,000).</p></div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Show the solution and the teaching</summary><div class="sol">
