<div class="diff"><b>What is different here:</b> Unlike Exercise 5, <b>two</b> projects qualify, so the question 'should we fund any of the others?' has the answer yes. Also notice Time Fades Away: it gets back exactly what it cost ($600,000) in year 1, which looks like an instant payback. But that $600,000 is worth only $500,000 in today's money at 20%, and the later flows are tiny. So it never truly earns the 20% required. This is a good example of why simple payback can mislead.</div>
