<section id="ch2-cheat" class="section-block">
<h3>Chapter 2 in one page (revise from this)</h3>
<div class="tablewrap"><table class="calc"><thead><tr><th class="l">Tool</th><th class="l">Formula</th><th class="l">Accept if</th><th class="l">Compare projects by</th><th class="l">Main weakness</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="l">Payback</td><td class="l">Cost ÷ annual flow, or running total</td><td class="l">Below the company's limit</td><td class="l">Lower is better</td><td class="l">Ignores time value (simple) and everything after payback</td></tr><tr><td class="l">Discounted payback</td><td class="l">Running total of PVs</td><td class="l">Below the limit</td><td class="l">Lower is better</td><td class="l">Still ignores flows after payback</td></tr><tr><td class="l">NPV</td><td class="l">I<sub>0</sub> + Σ F<sub>t</sub> ÷ (1+k)<sup>t</sup></td><td class="l">NPV &gt; 0</td><td class="l">Higher is better</td><td class="l">Needs a reliable discount rate</td></tr><tr><td class="l">IRR</td><td class="l">Rate where NPV = 0</td><td class="l">IRR &gt; required rate</td><td class="l">Higher is better</td><td class="l">Several IRRs if signs change more than once</td></tr><tr><td class="l">MIRR</td><td class="l">(FV of +) ÷ (PV of −), power 1/n, minus 1</td><td class="l">MIRR &gt; required rate</td><td class="l">Higher is better</td><td class="l">Needs two rate assumptions</td></tr><tr><td class="l">Profitability index</td><td class="l">PV of inflows ÷ investment</td><td class="l">PI &gt; 1</td><td class="l">Higher is better</td><td class="l">Ignores project size</td></tr><tr><td class="l">Weighted scoring</td><td class="l">Σ weight × rating</td><td class="l">Passes must gates</td><td class="l">Highest total</td><td class="l">Ratings and weights are judgment</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<aside class="callout exam"><p class="ct">Decision rules to write in the exam</p><ul>
<li>If NPV and payback disagree, <b>choose NPV</b> (it measures total value; payback measures speed).</li>
<li>If projects are ranked by "return on investment", use IRR or profitability index (rates), not raw NPV.</li>
<li>Screen with <b>must</b> criteria first (pass or fail), then score the <b>want</b> criteria.</li>
<li>Compliance is must-do, operational is efficiency, strategic is growth.</li>
</ul></aside>
<aside class="callout trap"><p class="ct">Common mistakes</p><ul>
<li>Writing the investment as a positive number in an NPV.</li>
<li>Discounting year 0 (its factor is exactly 1).</li>
<li>Using a percent like 18 instead of 0.18 in a formula.</li>
<li>Stopping the payback calculation at the wrong year: use the <i>running total</i>, not single years.</li>
<li>Forgetting extra items in a year (salvage, mid-life investment) when building the net cash flow.</li>
</ul></aside>
