<h4>Turn the wedding WBS into a network</h4>
<div class="restate"><p>Here is a partial work breakdown structure for a wedding (1.1 Decide on date; 1.2 Marriage license; 1.3 Ceremony [rent church, florist, create/print programs, hire photographer, wedding ceremony]; 1.4 Guests [develop guest list, order invitations, address and mail invitations, track RSVPs]; 1.5 Reception [reserve reception hall; food and beverage: choose caterer, decide on menu, make final order; hire DJ; decorate reception hall; wedding reception]). Use the yellow-sticky approach to create a network for this project. Do not include summary tasks, and do not consider who does the task.</p></div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Show the solution and the teaching</summary><div class="sol">
<h5>Step 1. Use the hint: start from the end and ask "what must be finished immediately before this?"</h5>
<p>The last activity is <b>R, the wedding reception</b>. Before it you need: the ceremony to be over (Q), the DJ hired (G), the food ordered (O) and the hall decorated (P). Then repeat for each of those.</p>
<ol class="steps"><li><b>Q, Wedding ceremony</b> needs the marriage license (B), the photographer hired (F), the florist done (I) and the programs printed (J).</li><li><b>I (florist) and J (programs)</b> both need the church to be rented first (C).</li><li><b>O, Make final order</b> needs the menu decided (N) and the number of guests confirmed (M, track RSVPs). M needs invitations mailed (L), which need invitations ordered (K), which need the guest list (E).</li><li><b>N (menu)</b> comes after choosing a caterer (H), which needs the reception hall reserved (D).</li><li><b>P, Decorate the hall</b> needs the hall reserved (D) and the flowers (I).</li><li>Almost everything begins after <b>A, decide on the date</b>, because you cannot book a church, hall or DJ without one.</li></ol>
