d" x="656.0" y="82.3" text-anchor="middle">E</text><text class="n" x="705.0" y="82.3" text-anchor="middle">14</text><text class="sl" x="607.0" y="105.0" text-anchor="middle">0</text><text class="nm" x="656.0" y="105.0" text-anchor="middle">Pour foundat…</text><text class="sl" x="705.0" y="105.0" text-anchor="middle">0</text><text class="n" x="607.0" y="127.7" text-anchor="middle">11</text><text class="du" x="656.0" y="127.7" text-anchor="middle">3</text><text class="n" x="705.0" y="127.7" text-anchor="middle">14</text></g></svg><p class="mini" style="margin:6px 8px 2px">Each box: <b>top row</b> ES | ID | EF, <b>middle row</b> start slack | activity | finish slack, <b>bottom row</b> LS | duration | LF. Red boxes and red arrows are the critical path.</p><figcaption>The completed network with early and late times</figcaption></figure><div class="final"><p class="ct">Final answer</p><p>Project duration = <b>14 days</b>.</p><p>Critical path: <b>A → B → D → E</b>.</p><p>Slack on the other activities: C = 2.</p></div><div class="diff"><b>What is different here:</b> this is the model question. Read it carefully once; every later question repeats these four steps. Notice that <b>C</b> is not critical: it takes 3 days, but D (5 days) runs in parallel, so C can slip 2 days without delaying E. That is what slack means.</div></div></details>
