<h4>Air Control Company: early, late and slack times</h4>
<div class="restate"><p>The project information for the custom order project of the Air Control Company is presented here. Draw a project network. Compute the early and late activity times and slack times. Identify the critical path.</p><div class="tablewrap"><table class="calc"><thead><tr><th class="c">ID</th><th class="l">Description</th><th class="l">Predecessor(s)</th><th class="r">Time (days)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="c">A</td><td class="l">Order review</td><td class="l">None</td><td class="r">2</td></tr><tr><td class="c">B</td><td class="l">Order standard parts</td><td class="l">A</td><td class="r">3</td></tr><tr><td class="c">C</td><td class="l">Produce standard parts</td><td class="l">A</td><td class="r">10</td></tr><tr><td class="c">D</td><td class="l">Design custom parts</td><td class="l">A</td><td class="r">13</td></tr><tr><td class="c">E</td><td class="l">Software development</td><td class="l">A</td><td class="r">18</td></tr><tr><td class="c">F</td><td class="l">Manufacture custom hardware</td><td class="l">C, D</td><td class="r">15</td></tr><tr><td class="c">G</td><td class="l">Assemble</td><td class="l">B, F</td><td class="r">10</td></tr><tr><td class="c">H</td><td class="l">Test</td><td class="l">E, G</td><td class="r">5</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Show the solution and the teaching</summary><div class="sol"><h5>Forward pass</h5><ul><li><b>A</b>: nothing comes before it, so ES = 0 and EF = 0 + 2 = <b>2</b>.</li><li><b>B</b>: comes after A (EF = 2), so ES = 2 and EF = 2 + 3 = <b>5</b>.</li><li><b>C</b>: comes after A (EF = 2), so ES = 2 and EF = 2 + 10 = <b>12</b>.</li><li><b>D</b>: comes after A (EF = 2), so ES = 2 and EF = 2 + 13 = <b>15</b>.</li><li><b>E</b>: comes after A (EF = 2), so ES = 2 and EF = 2 + 18 = <b>20</b>.</li><li><b>F</b> is a merge activity: it waits for C (EF = 12), D (EF = 15). ES = the <i>largest</i> = 15, EF = 15 + 15 = <b>30</b>.</li><li><b>G</b> is a merge activity: it waits for B (EF = 5), F (EF = 30). ES = the <i>largest</i> = 30, EF = 30 + 10 = <b>40</b>.</li><li><b>H</b> is a merge activity: it waits for E (EF = 20), G (EF = 40). ES = the <i>largest</i> = 40, EF = 40 + 5 = <b>45</b>.</li></ul><h5>Backward pass</h5><ul><li><b>H</b>: last activity, so LF = project length = 45. LS = 45 − 5 = <b>40</b>.</li><li><b>G</b>: only H follows it (LS = 40), so LF = 40. LS = 40 − 10 = <b>30</b>.</li><li><b>F</b>: only G follows it (LS = 30), so LF = 30. LS = 30 − 15 = <b>15</b>.</li><li><b>E</b>: only H follows it (LS = 40), so LF = 40. LS = 40 − 18 = <b>22</b>.</li><li><b>D</b>: only F follows it (LS = 15), so LF = 15. LS = 15 − 13 = <b>2</b>.</li><li><b>C</b>: only F follows it (LS = 15), so LF = 15. LS = 15 − 10 = <b>5</b>.</li><li><b>B</b>: only G follows it (LS = 30), so LF = 30. LS = 30 − 3 = <b>27</b>.</li><li><b>A</b> is a burst activity: B (LS = 27), C (LS = 5), D (LS = 2), E (LS = 22) follow it. LF = the <i>smallest</i> = 2. LS = 2 − 2 = <b>0</b>.</li></ul><h5>Slack, critical path and the completed network</h5><div class="tablewrap"><table class="calc"><thead><tr><th class="c">ID</th><th class="l">Activity</th><th class="r">Dur</th><th class="r">ES</th><th class="r">EF</th><th class="r">LS</th><th class="r">LF</th><th class="r">Total slack</th><th clas