<h4>The Simpsons' garage: bonus or penalty?</h4>
<div class="restate"><p>You have signed a contract to build a garage for the Simpsons. You receive a $500 bonus for completing within 17 working days and lose $100 for each day beyond 17. Draw the network, complete the forward and backward pass, compute slack and identify the critical path. Do you expect a bonus or a penalty?</p><div class="tablewrap"><table class="calc"><thead><tr><th class="c">ID</th><th class="l">Description</th><th class="l">Predecessor(s)</th><th class="r">Time (days)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="c">A</td><td class="l">Prepare site</td><td class="l">None</td><td class="r">2</td></tr><tr><td class="c">B</td><td class="l">Pour foundation</td><td class="l">A</td><td class="r">3</td></tr><tr><td class="c">C</td><td class="l">Erect frame</td><td class="l">B</td><td class="r">4</td></tr><tr><td class="c">D</td><td class="l">Roof</td><td class="l">C</td><td class="r">4</td></tr><tr><td class="c">E</td><td class="l">Windows</td><td class="l">C</td><td class="r">1</td></tr><tr><td class="c">F</td><td class="l">Doors</td><td class="l">C</td><td class="r">1</td></tr><tr><td class="c">G</td><td class="l">Electrical</td><td class="l">C</td><td class="r">3</td></tr><tr><td class="c">H</td><td class="l">Rough-in-frame</td><td class="l">D, E, F, G</td><td class="r">2</td></tr><tr><td class="c">I</td><td class="l">Door opener</td><td class="l">F, G</td><td class="r">1</td></tr><tr><td class="c">J</td><td class="l">Paint</td><td class="l">H, I</td><td class="r">2</td></tr><tr><td class="c">K</td><td class="l">Cleanup</td><td class="l">J</td><td class="r">1</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Show the solution and the teaching</summary><div class="sol"><h5>Forward pass</h5><ul><li><b>A</b>: nothing comes before it, so ES = 0 and EF = 0 + 2 = <b>2</b>.</li><li><b>B</b>: comes after A (EF = 2), so ES = 2 and EF = 2 + 3 = <b>5</b>.</li><li><b>C</b>: comes after B (EF = 5), so ES = 5 and EF = 5 + 4 = <b>9</b>.</li><li><b>D</b>: comes after C (EF = 9), so ES = 9 and EF = 9 + 4 = <b>13</b>.</li><li><b>E</b>: comes after C (EF = 9), so ES = 9 and EF = 9 + 1 = <b>10</b>.</li><li><b>F</b>: comes after C (EF = 9), so ES = 9 and EF = 9 + 1 = <b>10</b>.</li><li><b>G</b>: comes after C (EF = 9), so ES = 9 and EF = 9 + 3 = <b>12</b>.</li><li><b>H</b> is a merge activity: it waits for D (EF = 13), E (EF = 10), F (EF = 10), G (EF = 12). ES = the <i>largest</i> = 13, EF = 13 + 2 = <b>15</b>.</li><li><b>I</b> is a merge activity: it waits for F (EF = 10), G (EF = 12). ES = the <i>largest</i> = 12, EF = 12 + 1 = <b>13</b>.</li><li><b>J</b> is a merge activity: it waits for H (EF = 15), I (EF = 13). ES = the <i>largest</i> = 15, EF = 15 + 2 = <b>17</b>.</li><li><b>K</b>: comes after J (EF = 17), so ES = 17 and EF = 17 + 1 = <b>18</b>.</li></ul><h5>Backward pass</h5><ul><li><b>K</b>: last activity, so LF = project length = 18. LS = 18 − 1 = <b>17</b>.</li><li><b>J</b>: only K follows it (LS = 17), so LF = 17. LS = 17 − 2 = <b>15</b>.</li><li><b>I</b>: only J follows it (LS = 15), so LF = 15. LS = 15 − 1 = <b>14</b>.</li><li><b>H</b>: only J follows it (LS = 15), so LF = 15. LS = 15 − 2 = <b>13</b>.</li><li><b>G</b> is a burst activity: H (LS = 13), I (LS = 14) follow it. LF = the <i>smallest</i> = 13. LS = 13 − 3 = <b>10</b>.</li><li><b>F</b> is a burst activity: H (LS = 13), I (LS = 14) follow it. LF = the <i>smallest</i> = 13. LS = 13 − 1 = <b>12</b>.</li><li><b>E</b>: only H follows it (LS = 13), so LF = 13. LS = 13 − 1 = <b>12</b>.</li><li><b>D</b>: only H follows it (LS = 13), so LF = 13. LS = 13 − 4 = <b>9</b>.</li><li><b>C</b> is a bur