swer</p><p>Project duration = <b>10 days</b>.</p><p>Critical paths: <b>A → B → E → H → K → L &nbsp;and&nbsp; A → C → F → I → K → L &nbsp;and&nbsp; A → D → G → J → K → L</b>.</p></div><h5>How sensitive is the network?</h5><p><b>Every activity is critical</b>, and there are 3 critical paths (A → B → E → H → K → L; A → C → F → I → K → L; A → D → G → J → K → L). Any delay anywhere delays the project, so the network is <b>extremely sensitive</b>.</p><div class="diff"><b>What is different here:</b> all three branches (B-E-H, C-F-I and D-G-J) are exactly 4 days long, so <b>every activity is critical</b>. The question asks for the free and total slack of non-critical activities: there are none (all slack is 0). This is the most sensitive network possible.</div></div></details>
