estion and the book's own solution disagree on activity J</p><p>The question as printed gives Bid proposal (J) <b>10 days</b>, which makes the project <b>155 days</b> (critical path A-C-E-G-J = 5 + 30 + 80 + 30 + 10). But the solution in the book's Appendix One, and your professor's slide (which copies it), show J as <b>5 days</b> and a total of <b>150 days</b>. Everything else in their solution (ES, EF, LS, LF and slack for A to I, and the critical path A-C-E-G-J) matches the table below. So the book itself is inconsistent between the question and its answer (probably a different edition). <b>Rule for the exam: use the duration written in the question in front of you.</b> With J = 5 the answer is 150; with J = 10 it is 155.</p></aside></div></details>
