<h4>Choosing a software vendor</h4>
<div class="restate"><p>You are responsible for choosing a critical software product from competing vendors. Draw your project network, compute the activity early, late and slack times, and determine the critical path. How long will the project take? How sensitive is the network schedule?</p><div class="tablewrap"><table class="calc"><thead><tr><th class="c">ID</th><th class="l">Description</th><th class="l">Predecessor(s)</th><th class="r">Time (days)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="c">A</td><td class="l">Interview management</td><td class="l">None</td><td class="r">2</td></tr><tr><td class="c">B</td><td class="l">Interview operations</td><td class="l">None</td><td class="r">4</td></tr><tr><td class="c">C</td><td class="l">Interview technical staff</td><td class="l">None</td><td class="r">2</td></tr><tr><td class="c">D</td><td class="l">Prepare requirements document</td><td class="l">A, B, C</td><td class="r">2</td></tr><tr><td class="c">E</td><td class="l">Prepare request for proposal and transmit</td><td class="l">D</td><td class="r">2</td></tr><tr><td class="c">F</td><td class="l">Await receipt of proposals</td><td class="l">E</td><td class="r">14</td></tr><tr><td class="c">G</td><td class="l">Write acceptance criteria</td><td class="l">E</td><td class="r">2</td></tr><tr><td class="c">H</td><td class="l">Prototype solution</td><td class="l">E</td><td class="r">10</td></tr><tr><td class="c">I</td><td class="l">Test prototype</td><td class="l">H</td><td class="r">5</td></tr><tr><td class="c">J</td><td class="l">Develop project plan</td><td class="l">H</td><td class="r">3</td></tr><tr><td class="c">K</td><td class="l">Evaluate proposals</td><td class="l">F, G, I, J</td><td class="r">2</td></tr><tr><td class="c">L</td><td class="l">Request and receive final bid</td><td class="l">K</td><td class="r">1</td></tr><tr><td class="c">M</td><td class="l">Make vendor decision</td><td class="l">L</td><td class="r">1</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Show the solution and the teaching</summary><div class="sol"><h5>Forward pass</h5><ul><li><b>A</b>: nothing comes before it, so ES = 0 and EF = 0 + 2 = <b>2</b>.</li><li><b>B</b>: nothing comes before it, so ES = 0 and EF = 0 + 4 = <b>4</b>.</li><li><b>C</b>: nothing comes before it, so ES = 0 and EF = 0 + 2 = <b>2</b>.</li><li><b>D</b> is a merge activity: it waits for A (EF = 2), B (EF = 4), C (EF = 2). ES = the <i>largest</i> = 4, EF = 4 + 2 = <b>6</b>.</li><li><b>E</b>: comes after D (EF = 6), so ES = 6 and EF = 6 + 2 = <b>8</b>.</li><li><b>F</b>: comes after E (EF = 8), so ES = 8 and EF = 8 + 14 = <b>22</b>.</li><li><b>G</b>: comes after E (EF = 8), so ES = 8 and EF = 8 + 2 = <b>10</b>.</li><li><b>H</b>: comes after E (EF = 8), so ES = 8 and EF = 8 + 10 = <b>18</b>.</li><li><b>I</b>: comes after H (EF = 18), so ES = 18 and EF = 18 + 5 = <b>23</b>.</li><li><b>J</b>: comes after H (EF = 18), so ES = 18 and EF = 18 + 3 = <b>21</b>.</li><li><b>K</b> is a merge activity: it waits for F (EF = 22), G (EF = 10), I (EF = 23), J (EF = 21). ES = the <i>largest</i> = 23, EF = 23 + 2 = <b>25</b>.</li><li><b>L</b>: comes after K (EF = 25), so ES = 25 and EF = 25 + 1 = <b>26</b>.</li><li><b>M</b>: comes after L (EF = 26), so ES = 26 and EF = 26 + 1 = <b>27</b>.</li></ul><h5>Backward pass</h5><ul><li><b>M</b>: last activity, so LF = project length = 27. LS = 27 − 1 = <b>26</b>.</li><li><b>L</b>: only M follows it (LS = 26), so LF = 26. LS = 26 − 1 = <b>25</b>.</li><li><b>K</b>: only L follows it (LS = 25), so LF = 25. LS = 25 − 2 = <b>23</b>.</li><li><b>J</b>: only K follows it (LS = 23), so LF = 23. LS = 23 − 3 = <b>20</b>.</li><li><b>I</b>: only K follows it (LS = 23), so LF = 23. LS = 23 − 5 = <b>18</b>.</li><li><b>H</b> is a burst activity: I (LS = 18), J (LS = 20) follow it. LF = the <i>smallest</i> = 18. LS = 18 − 10 = <b>8</b>.</li><li><b>G</b>: only K follows it (LS = 23), so LF = 23. LS = 23 − 2 = <b>21</b>.</li><li><b>F</b>: only K follows it (LS = 23), so LF = 23. LS = 23 − 14 = <b>9</b>.</li><li><b>E</b> is a burst activity: F (LS = 9), G (LS = 21), H (LS = 8) follow it. LF = the <i>smallest</i> = 8. LS = 8 − 2 = <b>6</b>.</li><li><b>D</b>: only E follows it (LS = 6), so LF = 6. LS = 6 − 2 = <b>4</b>.</li><li><b>C</b>: only D follows it (LS = 4), so LF = 4. LS = 4 − 2 = <b>2</b>.</li><li><b>B</b>: only D follows it (LS = 4), so LF = 4. LS = 4 − 4 = <b>0</b>.</li><li><b>A</b>: only D follows it (LS = 4), so LF = 4. LS = 4 − 2 = <b>2</b>.</li></ul><h5>Slack, critical path and the completed network</h5><div class="tablewrap"><table class="calc"><thead><tr><th class="c">ID</th><th class="l">Activity</th><th class="r">Dur</th><th class="r">ES</th><th class="r">EF</th><th class="r">LS</th><th class="r">LF</th><th class="r">Total slack</th><th class="r">Free slack</th><th class="l"></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="c">A</td><td class="l">Interview management</td><td class="r">2</td><td class="r">0</td><td class="r">2</td><td class="r">2</td><td class="r">4</td><td class="r">2</td><td class="r">2</td><td class="l"></td></tr><tr class="hl"><td class="c">B</td><td class="l">Interview operations</td><td class="r">4</td><td class="r">0</td><td class="r">4</td><td class="r">0</td><td class="r">4</td><td class="r">0</td><td class="r">0</td><td class="l">Critical</td></tr><tr><td class="c">C</td><td class="l">Interview technical staff</td><td class="r">2</td><td class="r">0</td><td class="r">2</td><td class="r">2</td><td class="r">4</td><td class="r">2</td><td class="r">2</td><td class="l"></td></tr><tr class="hl"><td class="c">D</td><td class="l">Prepare requirements document</td><td class="r">2</td><td class="r">4</td><td class="r">6</td><td class="r">4</td><td class="r">6</td><td class="r">0</td><td class="r">0</td><td class="l">Critical</td></tr><tr class="hl"><td class="c">E</td><td class="l">Prepare request for proposal and transmit</td><td class="r">2</td><td class="r">6</td><td class="r">8</td>