<h4>MP4 player project: can it finish in 45 weeks?</h4>
<div class="restate"><p>The Planning Department of an electronics firm has set up the activities for developing a new MP4 player. Develop a project network (in Microsoft Project). Assume a five-day workweek and that the project starts on January 6, 2025. The team asks you to create a network and determine if the project can be completed in 45 weeks.</p><div class="tablewrap"><table class="calc"><thead><tr><th class="c">ID</th><th class="l">Description</th><th class="l">Predecessor(s)</th><th class="r">Time (weeks)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="c">1</td><td class="l">Staff</td><td class="l">None</td><td class="r">2</td></tr><tr><td class="c">2</td><td class="l">Develop market program</td><td class="l">1</td><td class="r">3</td></tr><tr><td class="c">3</td><td class="l">Select channels of distribution</td><td class="l">1</td><td class="r">8</td></tr><tr><td class="c">4</td><td class="l">Patent</td><td class="l">1</td><td class="r">12</td></tr><tr><td class="c">5</td><td class="l">Pilot production</td><td class="l">1</td><td class="r">4</td></tr><tr><td class="c">6</td><td class="l">Test market</td><td class="l">5</td><td class="r">4</td></tr><tr><td class="c">7</td><td class="l">Ad promotion</td><td class="l">2</td><td class="r">4</td></tr><tr><td class="c">8</td><td class="l">Set up for production</td><td class="l">4, 6</td><td class="r">16</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Show the solution and the teaching</summary><div class="sol"><h5>Forward pass</h5><ul><li><b>1</b>: nothing comes before it, so ES = 0 and EF = 0 + 2 = <b>2</b>.</li><li><b>2</b>: comes after 1 (EF = 2), so ES = 2 and EF = 2 + 3 = <b>5</b>.</li><li><b>3</b>: comes after 1 (EF = 2), so ES = 2 and EF = 2 + 8 = <b>10</b>.</li><li><b>4</b>: comes after 1 (EF = 2), so ES = 2 and EF = 2 + 12 = <b>14</b>.</li><li><b>5</b>: comes after 1 (EF = 2), so ES = 2 and EF = 2 + 4 = <b>6</b>.</li><li><b>6</b>: comes after 5 (EF = 6), so ES = 6 and EF = 6 + 4 = <b>10</b>.</li><li><b>7</b>: comes after 2 (EF = 5), so ES = 5 and EF = 5 + 4 = <b>9</b>.</li><li><b>8</b> is a merge activity: it waits for 4 (EF = 14), 6 (EF = 10). ES = the <i>largest</i> = 14, EF = 14 + 16 = <b>30</b>.</li></ul><h5>Backward pass</h5><ul><li><b>8</b>: last activity, so LF = project length = 30. LS = 30 − 16 = <b>14</b>.</li><li><b>7</b>: last activity, so LF = project length = 30. LS = 30 − 4 = <b>26</b>.</li><li><b>6</b>: only 8 follows it (LS = 14), so LF = 14. LS = 14 − 4 = <b>10</b>.</li><li><b>5</b>: only 6 follows it (LS = 10), so LF = 10. LS = 10 − 4 = <b>6</b>.</li><li><b>4</b>: only 8 follows it (LS = 14), so LF = 14. LS = 14 − 12 = <b>2</b>.</li><li><b>3</b>: last activity, so LF = project length = 30. LS = 30 − 8 = <b>22</b>.</li><li><b>2</b>: only 7 follows it (LS = 26), so LF = 26. LS = 26 − 3 = <b>23</b>.</li><li><b>1</b> is a burst activity: 2 (LS = 23), 3 (LS = 22), 4 (LS = 2), 5 (LS = 6) follow it. LF = the <i>smallest</i> = 2. LS = 2 − 2 = <b>0</b>.</li></ul><h5>Slack, critical path and the completed network</h5><div class="tablewrap"><table class="calc"><thead><tr><th class="c">ID</th><th class="l">Activity</th><th class="r">Dur</th><th class="r">ES</th><th class="r">EF</th><th class="r">LS</th><th class="r">LF</th><th class="r">Total slack</th><th class="r">Free slack</th><th class="l"></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class="hl"><td class="c">1</td><td class=