<h4>Group term paper: network and Gantt chart</h4>
<div class="restate"><p>You are completing a group term paper. Given the project network, complete the forward and backward pass, compute activity slack, and identify the critical path. Use this information to create a Gantt chart for the project. Be sure to show slack for noncritical activities.</p><div class="tablewrap"><table class="calc"><thead><tr><th class="c">ID</th><th class="l">Description</th><th class="l">Predecessor(s)</th><th class="r">Time (days)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="c">A</td><td class="l">Identify topic</td><td class="l">None</td><td class="r">1</td></tr><tr><td class="c">B</td><td class="l">Research topic</td><td class="l">A</td><td class="r">5</td></tr><tr><td class="c">C</td><td class="l">Draft paper</td><td class="l">B</td><td class="r">3</td></tr><tr><td class="c">D</td><td class="l">Edit paper</td><td class="l">C</td><td class="r">2</td></tr><tr><td class="c">E</td><td class="l">Create graphics</td><td class="l">C</td><td class="r">1</td></tr><tr><td class="c">F</td><td class="l">References</td><td class="l">C</td><td class="r">1</td></tr><tr><td class="c">G</td><td class="l">Proof</td><td class="l">D, E, F</td><td class="r">1</td></tr><tr><td class="c">H</td><td class="l">Submit paper</td><td class="l">G</td><td class="r">1</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Show the solution and the teaching</summary><div class="sol"><h5>Step 1. Read the table and find the starts, ends, bursts and merges</h5>
<p>Each row tells you one activity, how long it takes, and what must be finished before it can start. Activities with "None" are <b>starting activities</b>; an activity that no one else waits for is an <b>ending activity</b>.</p>
<ul><li>Burst activities (more than one follower): <b>C</b> (followed by D, E, F).</li><li>Merge activities (more than one predecessor): <b>G</b> (waits for D, E, F).</li></ul><h5>Step 2. Forward pass (earliest start and earliest finish)</h5><p>Start at zero. ES = the largest EF of the predecessors (only the last predecessor to finish matters), EF = ES + duration.</p><ul><li><b>A</b>: nothing comes before it, so ES = 0 and EF = 0 + 1 = <b>1</b>.</li><li><b>B</b>: comes after A (EF = 1), so ES = 1 and EF = 1 + 5 = <b>6</b>.</li><li><b>C</b>: comes after B (EF = 6), so ES = 6 and EF = 6 + 3 = <b>9</b>.</li><li><b>D</b>: comes after C (EF = 9), so ES = 9 and EF = 9 + 2 = <b>11</b>.</li><li><b>E</b>: comes after C (EF = 9), so ES = 9 and EF = 9 + 1 = <b>10</b>.</li><li><b>F</b>: comes after C (EF = 9), so ES = 9 and EF = 9 + 1 = <b>10</b>.</li><li><b>G</b> is a merge activity: it waits for D (EF = 11), E (EF = 10), F (EF = 10). ES = the <i>largest</i> = 11, EF = 11 + 1 = <b>12</b>.</li><li><b>H</b>: comes after G (EF = 12), so ES = 12 and EF = 12 + 1 = <b>13</b>.</li></ul><h5>Step 3. Backward pass (latest start and latest finish)</h5><p>Start at the end with LF = the project length. LS = LF − duration. For a burst activity use the smallest LS of its followers.</p><ul><li><b>H</b>: last activity, so LF = project length = 13. LS = 13 − 1 = <b>12</b>.</li><li><b>G</b>: only H follows it (LS = 12), so LF = 12. LS = 12 − 1 = <b>11</b>.</li><li><b>F</b>: only G follows it (LS = 11), so LF = 11. LS = 11 − 1 = <b>10</b>.</li><li><b>E</b>: only G follows it (LS = 11), so LF = 11. LS = 11 − 1 = <b>10</b>.</li><li><b>D</b>: only G follows it (LS = 11), so LF = 11. LS = 11 − 2 = <b>9</b>.</li><li><b>C</b> is a burst activity: D (LS = 9), E (LS = 10), F (LS = 10) follow it. LF = the <i>smallest</i> = 9. LS = 9 − 3 = <b>6</b>.</li><li><b>B</b>: only C follows it (LS = 6), so LF = 6. LS = 6 − 5 = <b>1</b>.</li><li><b>A</b>: only B follows it (LS = 1), so LF = 1. LS = 1 − 1 = <b>0</b>.</li></ul><h5>Step 4. Slack, critical path and the completed network</h5><p>Total slack = LS − ES. Slack 0 means critical. Free slack = the smallest ES of the followers minus this activity's EF.</p><div class="tablewrap"><table class="calc"><thead><tr><th class="c">ID</th><th class="l">Activity</th><th class="r">Dur</th><th class="r">ES</th><th class="r">EF</th><th class="r">LS</th><th class="r">LF</th><th class="r">Total slack</th><th class="r">Free slack</th><th class="l"></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class="hl"><td class="c">A</td><td class="l">Identify topic</td><td class="r">1</td><td class="r">0</td><td class="r">1</td><td class="r">0</td><td class="r">1</td><td class="r">0</td><td class="r">0</td><td class="l">Critical</td></tr><tr class="hl"><td class="c">B</td><td class="l">Research topic</td><td class="r">5</td><td class="r">1</td><td class="r">6</td><td class="r">1</td><td class="r">6</td><td class="r">0</td><td class="r">0</td><td class="l">Critical</td></tr><tr class="hl"><td class="c">C</td><td class="l">Draft paper</td><td class="r">3</td><td class="r">6</td><td class="r">9</td><td class="r">6</td><td class="r">9</td><td class="r">0</td><td class="r">0</td><td class="l">Critical</td></tr><tr class="hl"><td class="c">D</td><td class="l">Edit paper</td><td class="r">2</td><td class="r">9</td><td class="r">11</td><td class="r">9</td><td class="r">11</td><td class="r">0</td><td class="r">0</td><td class="l">Critical</td></tr><tr><td class="c">E</td><td class="l">Create graphics</td><td class="r">1</td><td class="r">9</td><td class="r">10</td><td class="r">10</td><td class="r">11</td><td class="r">1</td><td class="r">1</td><td class="l"></td></tr><tr><td class="c">F</td><td class="l">References</td><td class="r">1</td><td class="r">9</td><td class="r">10</td><td class="r">10</td><td class="r">11</td><td class="r">1</td><td class="r">1</td><td class="l"></td></tr><tr class="hl"><td class="c">G</td><td class="l">Proof</td><td class="r">1</td><td class="r">11<