<h4>Bangkokagogo product upgrade: network and Gantt chart</h4>
<div class="restate"><p>You are managing a product upgrade project for Bangkokagogo. Given the project network, complete the forward and backward pass, compute activity slack, and identify the critical path. Use this information to create a Gantt chart for the project. Be sure to show slack for noncritical activities.</p><div class="tablewrap"><table class="calc"><thead><tr><th class="c">ID</th><th class="l">Description</th><th class="l">Predecessor(s)</th><th class="r">Time (weeks)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="c">A</td><td class="l">Form project team</td><td class="l">None</td><td class="r">1</td></tr><tr><td class="c">B</td><td class="l">Interview users</td><td class="l">A</td><td class="r">5</td></tr><tr><td class="c">C</td><td class="l">Survey users</td><td class="l">A</td><td class="r">3</td></tr><tr><td class="c">D</td><td class="l">Identify new features</td><td class="l">B, C</td><td class="r">2</td></tr><tr><td class="c">E</td><td class="l">Acquire materials</td><td class="l">D</td><td class="r">4</td></tr><tr><td class="c">F</td><td class="l">Develop marketing campaign</td><td class="l">D</td><td class="r">2</td></tr><tr><td class="c">G</td><td class="l">Produce prototypes</td><td class="l">E</td><td class="r">3</td></tr><tr><td class="c">H</td><td class="l">Design graphics</td><td class="l">D</td><td class="r">3</td></tr><tr><td class="c">I</td><td class="l">Conduct marketing</td><td class="l">F</td><td class="r">5</td></tr><tr><td class="c">J</td><td class="l">Perform sales calls</td><td class="l">G, H, I</td><td class="r">3</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Show the solution and the teaching</summary><div class="sol"><h5>Forward pass</h5><ul><li><b>A</b>: nothing comes before it, so ES = 0 and EF = 0 + 1 = <b>1</b>.</li><li><b>B</b>: comes after A (EF = 1), so ES = 1 and EF = 1 + 5 = <b>6</b>.</li><li><b>C</b>: comes after A (EF = 1), so ES = 1 and EF = 1 + 3 = <b>4</b>.</li><li><b>D</b> is a merge activity: it waits for B (EF = 6), C (EF = 4). ES = the <i>largest</i> = 6, EF = 6 + 2 = <b>8</b>.</li><li><b>E</b>: comes after D (EF = 8), so ES = 8 and EF = 8 + 4 = <b>12</b>.</li><li><b>F</b>: comes after D (EF = 8), so ES = 8 and EF = 8 + 2 = <b>10</b>.</li><li><b>G</b>: comes after E (EF = 12), so ES = 12 and EF = 12 + 3 = <b>15</b>.</li><li><b>H</b>: comes after D (EF = 8), so ES = 8 and EF = 8 + 3 = <b>11</b>.</li><li><b>I</b>: comes after F (EF = 10), so ES = 10 and EF = 10 + 5 = <b>15</b>.</li><li><b>J</b> is a merge activity: it waits for G (EF = 15), H (EF = 11), I (EF = 15). ES = the <i>largest</i> = 15, EF = 15 + 3 = <b>18</b>.</li></ul><h5>Backward pass</h5><ul><li><b>J</b>: last activity, so LF = project length = 18. LS = 18 − 3 = <b>15</b>.</li><li><b>I</b>: only J follows it (LS = 15), so LF = 15. LS = 15 − 5 = <b>10</b>.</li><li><b>H</b>: only J follows it (LS = 15), so LF = 15. LS = 15 − 3 = <b>12</b>.</li><li><b>G</b>: only J follows it (LS = 15), so LF = 15. LS = 15 − 3 = <b>12</b>.</li><li><b>F</b>: only I follows it (LS = 10), so LF = 10. LS = 10 − 2 = <b>8</b>.</li><li><b>E</b>: only G follows it (LS = 12), so LF = 12. LS = 12 − 4 = <b>8</b>.</li><li><b>D</b> is a burst activity: E (LS = 8), F (LS = 8), H (LS = 12) follow it. LF = the <i>smallest</i> = 8. LS = 8 − 2 = <b>6</b>.</li><li><b>C</b>: only D follows it (LS = 6), so LF = 6. LS = 6 − 3 = <b>3</b>.</li><li><b>B</b>: only D follows it (LS = 6), so LF = 6. LS = 6 − 5 = <b>1</b>.</li><li><b>A</b> is a burst activity: B (LS = 1), C (LS = 3) follow it. LF = the <i>smallest</i> = 1. LS = 1 − 1 = <b>0</b>.</li></ul><