<h4>Warm-up: laddering and start-to-start lags</h4>
<div class="restate"><p>(1) Activities A (3 days), B (6) and C (9) are done one after another. Show how laddering or lags reduce the time. (2) Dig trench (6 days), Lay cable (3 days, SS+1 and FF+1 with dig), Back fill (2 days, SS+1 and FF+1 with lay cable): find the duration and which activities are critical only at the finish.</p></div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Show the solution and the teaching</summary><div class="sol">
<h5>Part 1. Laddering</h5>
<p><b>In a row (finish to start):</b> 3 + 6 + 9 = <b>18 days</b>.</p>
<p><b>Laddered:</b> cut every job into three equal segments (A: 1 day each, B: 2 days each, C: 3 days each). The next job starts as soon as its first segment can. A finishes at day 3, B's first segment can start at day 1, C's first segment at day 3, so C's last segment ends at 3 + 9 = <b>12 days</b>.</p>
<p><b>The same thing written with lags:</b> B is SS+1 after A, and C is SS+2 after B.</p>
