<h4>Interview to field test with lags</h4>
<div class="restate"><p>Given the information in the lag exercise (A Interview 15, B Define new features 5, C Order components 2, D Prototype 8, E Test 5, F Field test 10, with the lags shown), compute the early, late and slack times. Which activities on the critical path have only the start or finish of the activity on the critical path?</p></div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Show the solution and the teaching</summary><div class="sol"><p><b>Reading the picture:</b> A to B has two arrows: a start-to-start "Lag 10" (B can start 10 after A starts) and a finish-to-finish "Lag 3" (B cannot finish until 3 after A finishes). B to C is plain. C to D: FS+5. C to E: FS+4. E to F: FS+3. D to F plain.</p><h5>The relationships</h5><div class="tablewrap"><table class="calc"><thead><tr><th class="c">ID</th><th class="l">Description</th><th class="l">Predecessor(s)</th><th class="r">Time (days)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="c">A</td><td class="l">Interview</td><td class="l">None</td><td class="r">15</td></tr><tr><td class="c">B</td><td class="l">Def. new features</td><td class="l">A (SS+10), A (FF+3)</td><td class="r">5</td></tr><tr><td class="c">C</td><td class="l">Order comps</td><td class="l">B</td><td class="r">2</td></tr><tr><td class="c">D</td><td class="l">Prototype</td><td class="l">C (FS+5)</td><td class="r">8</td></tr><tr><td class="c">E</td><td class="l">Test</td><td class="l">C (FS+4)</td><td class="r">5</td></tr><tr><td class="c">F</td><td class="l">Field test</td><td class="l">D, E (FS+3)</td><td class="r">10</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h5>Forward pass</h5><ul><li><b>A</b>: nothing comes before it, so ES = 0 and EF = 0 + 15 = <b>15</b>.</li><li><b>B</b> (A SS+10: ES 0+10 = 10 (start); A FF+3: EF 15+3 = 18 (finish)). ES = 10. EF = the larger of ES + duration = 10 + 5 = 15 and the finish limit 18 = <b>18</b>.</li><li><b>C</b> (B FS: EF 18 = 18 (start)). ES = 18. EF = the larger of ES + duration = 18 + 2 = 20 = <b>20</b>.</li><li><b>D</b> (C FS+5: EF 20+5 = 25 (start)). ES = 25. EF = the larger of ES + duration = 25 + 8 = 33 = <b>33</b>.</li><li><b>E</b> (C FS+4: EF 20+4 = 24 (start)). ES = 24. EF = the larger of ES + duration = 24 + 5 = 29 = <b>29</b>.</li><li><b>F</b> (D FS: EF 33 = 33 (start); E FS+3: EF 29+3 = 32 (start)). ES = 33 (largest start limit). EF = the larger of ES + duration = 33 + 10 = 43 = <b>43</b>.</li></ul><h5>Backward pass</h5><ul><li><b>F</b>: last activity, so LF = project length = 43. LS = 43 − 10 = <b>33</b>.</li><li><b>E</b> (F FS+3: LS 33-3 = 30 (finish limit)). LF = <b>30</b>, LS = <b>25</b>.</li><li><b>D</b> (F FS+0: LS 33+0 = 33 (finish limit)). LF = <b>33</b>, LS = <b>25</b>.</li><li><b>C</b> (D FS+5: LS 25-5 = 20 (finish limit); E FS+4: LS 25-4 = 21 (finish limit)). LF = <b>20</b>, LS = <b>18</b>.</li><li><b>B</b> (C FS+0: LS 18+0 = 18 (finish limit)). LF = <b>18</b>, LS = <b>13</b>.</li><li><b>A</b> (B SS+10: LS 13-10 = 3 (start limit); B FF+3: LF 18-3 = 15 (finish limit)). LF = <b>15</b>, LS = <b>0</b>.</li></ul><h5>Start slack, finish slack and the completed network</h5><p>Start slack = LS − ES. Finish slack = LF − EF. An activity is critical if either is zero.</p><div class="tablewrap"><table class="calc"><thead><tr><th class="c">ID</th><th class="l">Activity</th><th class="r">Dur</th><th class="r">ES</th><th class="r">EF</th><th class="r">LS</th><th class="r">LF</th><th class="r">Start slack</th><th class="r">Finish slack</th><th class="l"></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class="hl"><td class="c">A</td><td class="l">Interview</td><td class="r">15</td><td class="r">0</td><td class="r">15</td><td class="r">0</td><td class="r">15</td><td class="r">0</td><td class="r">0</td><td class="l">Critical</td></tr><tr class="hl"><td class="c">B</td><td class="l">Def. new features</td><td class="r">5</td><td class="r">10</td><td class="r">18</td><td class="r">13</td><td class="r">18</td><td class="r">3</td><td class="r">0</td><td class="l">Critical</td></tr><tr class="hl"><td class="c">C</td><td class="l">Order comps</td><td class="r">2</td><td class="r">18</td><td class="r">20</td><td class="r">18</td><td class="r">20</td><td class="r">0</td><td class="r">0</td><td class="l">Critical</td></tr><tr class="hl"><td class="c">D</td><td class="l">Prototype</td><td class="r">8</td><td class="r">25</td><td class="r">33</td><td class="r">25</td><