<h4>Cabinets and appliances with lags</h4>
<div class="restate"><p>Given the network (A Design 3, B Tear Down 3, C Order Appliances 1, D Build Cabinets 7, E Install Cabinets 2, F Install Appliances 2, G Inspect 1, with the lags shown), compute the early, late and slack time for each activity. Clearly identify the critical path.</p></div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Show the solution and the teaching</summary><div class="sol"><p><b>Reading the picture (checked against the professor's solution):</b> A to B: SS+2. A to C and A to D: plain. D to E: two arrows, SS+5 and FF+1. B to E plain. C to F: FS+5. E to F and F to G plain.</p><h5>The relationships</h5><div class="tablewrap"><table class="calc"><thead><tr><th class="c">ID</th><th class="l">Description</th><th class="l">Predecessor(s)</th><th class="r">Time (days)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="c">A</td><td class="l">Design</td><td class="l">None</td><td class="r">3</td></tr><tr><td class="c">B</td><td class="l">Tear down</td><td class="l">A (SS+2)</td><td class="r">3</td></tr><tr><td class="c">C</td><td class="l">Order appliances</td><td class="l">A</td><td class="r">1</td></tr><tr><td class="c">D</td><td class="l">Build cabinets</td><td class="l">A</td><td class="r">7</td></tr><tr><td class="c">E</td><td class="l">Install cabinets</td><td class="l">B, D (SS+5), D (FF+1)</td><td class="r">2</td></tr><tr><td class="c">F</td><td class="l">Install appliances</td><td class="l">E, C (FS+5)</td><td class="r">2</td></tr><tr><td class="c">G</td><td class="l">Inspect</td><td class="l">F</td><td class="r">1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h5>Forward pass</h5><ul><li><b>A</b>: nothing comes before it, so ES = 0 and EF = 0 + 3 = <b>3</b>.</li><li><b>B</b> (A SS+2: ES 0+2 = 2 (start)). ES = 2. EF = the larger of ES + duration = 2 + 3 = 5 = <b>5</b>.</li><li><b>C</b> (A FS: EF 3 = 3 (start)). ES = 3. EF = the larger of ES + duration = 3 + 1 = 4 = <b>4</b>.</li><li><b>D</b> (A FS: EF 3 = 3 (start)). ES = 3. EF = the larger of ES + duration = 3 + 7 = 10 = <b>10</b>.</li><li><b>E</b> (B FS: EF 5 = 5 (start); D SS+5: ES 3+5 = 8 (start); D FF+1: EF 10+1 = 11 (finish)). ES = 8 (largest start limit). EF = the larger of ES + duration = 8 + 2 = 10 and the finish limit 11 = <b>11</b>.</li><li><b>F</b> (E FS: EF 11 = 11 (start); C FS+5: EF 4+5 = 9 (start)). ES = 11 (largest start limit). EF = the larger of ES + duration = 11 + 2 = 13 = <b>13</b>.</li><li><b>G</b> (F FS: EF 13 = 13 (start)). ES = 13. EF = the larger of ES + duration = 13 + 1 = 14 = <b>14</b>.</li></ul><h5>Backward pass</h5><ul><li><b>G</b>: last activity, so LF = project length = 14. LS = 14 − 1 = <b>13</b>.</li><li><b>F</b> (G FS+0: LS 13+0 = 13 (finish limit)). LF = <b>13</b>, LS = <b>11</b>.</li><li><b>E</b> (F FS+0: LS 11+0 = 11 (finish limit)). LF = <b>11</b>, LS = <b>9</b>.</li><li><b>D</b> (E SS+5: LS 9-5 = 4 (start limit); E FF+1: LF 11-1 = 10 (finish limit)). LF = <b>10</b>, LS = <b>3</b>.</li><li><b>C</b> (F FS+5: LS 11-5 = 6 (finish limit)). LF = <b>6</b>, LS = <b>5</b>.</li><li><b>B</b> (E FS+0: LS 9+0 = 9 (finish limit)). LF = <b>9</b>, LS = <b>6</b>.</li><li><b>A</b> (B SS+2: LS 6-2 = 4 (start limit); C FS+0: LS 5+0 = 5 (finish limit); D FS+0: LS 3+0 = 3 (finish limit)). LF = <b>3</b>, LS = <b>0</b>.</li></ul><h5>Start slack, finish slack and the completed network</h5><p>Start slack = LS − ES. Finish slack = LF − EF. An activity is critical if either is zero.</p><div class="tablewrap"><table class="calc"><thead><tr><th class="c">ID</th><th class="l">Activity</th><th class="r">Dur</th><th class="r">ES</th><th class="r">EF</th><th class="r">LS</th><th class="r">LF</th><th class="r">Start slack</th><th class="r">Finish slack</th><th class="l"></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class="hl"><td class="c">A</td><td class="l">Design</td><td class="r">3</td><td class="r">0</td><td class="r">3</td><td class="r">0</td><td class="r">3</td><td class="r">0</td><td class="r">0</td><td class="l">Critical</td></tr><tr><td class="c">B</td><td class="l">Tear down</td><td class="r">3</td><td class="r">2</td><td class="r">5</td><td class="r">6</td><td class="r">9</td><td class="r">4</td><td class="r">4</td><td class="l"></td></tr><tr><td class="c">C</td><td class="l">Order appliances</td><td class="r">1</td><td class="r">3</td><td class="r">4</td><td class="r">5</td><td