>bottom row</b> LS | duration | LF. Red boxes and red arrows are the critical path.</p><figcaption>Completed network: orange arrows carry a lag or lead, red arrows are the critical links</figcaption></figure><div class="final"><p class="ct">Final answer</p><p>Project duration = <b>18 time units</b>.</p><p>Critical path: <b>A →[SS+2] D → F →[FF+3] G →[FS+4] J &nbsp;and&nbsp; A →[SS+2] D → F → I →[FF+5] J</b>.</p><p>Critical for only the start or only the finish: <b>A</b> (start only), <b>G</b> (finish only).</p></div><div class="diff"><b>What is different here:</b> G has ES = 6 (from C: 4 + 2) but EF = 12 (from F: 9 + 3), not 6 + 4 = 10. That is why G's start slack is 2 and its finish slack is 0. The fill-in answers on the slide follow from this table: ES of C = 1, LS of E = 11, LS of G = 8, start slack of G = 2, of B = 5, of E = 4, finish slack of H = 4, of F = 0, of G = 0.</div></div></details>
