<h4>Parking lot project with start-to-start lags</h4>
<div class="restate"><p>Given the network (Post signs 1, Prepare site 3, Lights 1, Dig trenches 5, Lay pipe 5, Back fill 3, Pave 2, Paint parking lines 1, Signage 1, Open lot 1, with lags A→B 10, D→E 3, E→F 3, G→H 1), compute the early, late and slack times. Which activities on the critical path have only the start or finish of the activity on the critical path?</p></div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Show the solution and the teaching</summary><div class="sol"><p><b>Reading the picture:</b> A to B: Lag 10 (FS+10, for example sign permits). D to E and E to F: Lag 3 drawn from the start of each box (SS+3). F to G plain; G to H: Lag 1 (FS+1). C, H and I feed J.</p><h5>The relationships</h5><div class="tablewrap"><table class="calc"><thead><tr><th class="c">ID</th><th class="l">Description</th><th class="l">Predecessor(s)</th><th class="r">Time (days)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="c">A</td><td class="l">Post signs</td><td class="l">None</td><td class="r">1</td></tr><tr><td class="c">B</td><td class="l">Prepare site</td><td class="l">A (FS+10)</td><td class="r">3</td></tr><tr><td class="c">C</td><td class="l">Lights</td><td class="l">B</td><td class="r">1</td></tr><tr><td class="c">D</td><td class="l">Dig trenches</td><td class="l">B</td><td class="r">5</td></tr><tr><td class="c">E</td><td class="l">Lay pipe</td><td class="l">D (SS+3)</td><td class="r">5</td></tr><tr><td class="c">F</td><td class="l">Back fill</td><td class="l">E (SS+3)</td><td class="r">3</td></tr><tr><td class="c">G</td><td class="l">Pave</td><td class="l">F</td><td class="r">2</td></tr><tr><td class="c">H</td><td class="l">Paint parking lines</td><td class="l">G (FS+1)</td><td class="r">1</td></tr><tr><td class="c">I</td><td class="l">Signage</td><td class="l">G</td><td class="r">1</td></tr><tr><td class="c">J</td><td class="l">Open lot</td><td class="l">C, H, I</td><td class="r">1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h5>Forward pass</h5><ul><li><b>A</b>: nothing comes before it, so ES = 0 and EF = 0 + 1 = <b>1</b>.</li><li><b>B</b> (A FS+10: EF 1+10 = 11 (start)). ES = 11. EF = the larger of ES + duration = 11 + 3 = 14 = <b>14</b>.</li><li><b>C</b> (B FS: EF 14 = 14 (start)). ES = 14. EF = the larger of ES + duration = 14 + 1 = 15 = <b>15</b>.</li><li><b>D</b> (B FS: EF 14 = 14 (start)). ES = 14. EF = the larger of ES + duration = 14 + 5 = 19 = <b>19</b>.</li><li><b>E</b> (D SS+3: ES 14+3 = 17 (start)). ES = 17. EF = the larger of ES + duration = 17 + 5 = 22 = <b>22</b>.</li><li><b>F</b> (E SS+3: ES 17+3 = 20 (start)). ES = 20. EF = the larger of ES + duration = 20 + 3 = 23 = <b>23</b>.</li><li><b>G</b> (F FS: EF 23 = 23 (start)). ES = 23. EF = the larger of ES + duration = 23 + 2 = 25 = <b>25</b>.</li><li><b>H</b> (G FS+1: EF 25+1 = 26 (start)). ES = 26. EF = the larger of ES + duration = 26 + 1 = 27 = <b>27</b>.</li><li><b>I</b> (G FS: EF 25 = 25 (start)). ES = 25. EF = the larger of ES + duration = 25 + 1 = 26 = <b>26</b>.</li><li><b>J</b> (C FS: EF 15 = 15 (start); H FS: EF 27 = 27 (start); I FS: EF 26 = 26 (start)). ES = 27 (largest start limit). EF = the larger of ES + duration = 27 + 1 = 28 = <b>28</b>.</li></ul><h5>Backward pass</h5><ul><li><b>J</b>: last activity, so LF = project length = 28. LS = 28 − 1 = <b>27</b>.</li><li><b>I</b> (J FS+0: LS 27+0 = 27 (finish limit)). LF = <b>27</b>, LS = <b>26</b>.</li><li><b>H</b> (J FS+0: LS 27+0 = 27 (finish limit)). LF = <b>27</b>, LS = <b>26</b>.</li><li><b>G</b> (H FS+1: LS 26-1 = 25 (finish limit); I FS+0: LS 26+0 = 26 (finish limit)). LF = <b>25</b>, LS = <b>23</b>.</li><li><b>F</b> (G FS+0: LS 23+0 = 23 (finish limit)). LF = <b>23</b>, LS = <b>20</b>.</li><li><b>E</b> (F SS+3: LS 20-3 = 17 (start limit)). LF = <b>28</b>, LS = <b>17</b>.</li><li><b>D</b> (E SS+3: LS 17-3 = 14 (start limit)). LF = <b>28</b>, LS = <b>14</b>.</li><li><b>C</b> (J FS+0: LS 27+0 = 27 (finish limit)). LF = <b>27</b>, LS = <b>26</b>.</li><li><b>B</b> (C FS+0: LS 26+0 = 26 (finish limit); D FS+0: LS 14+0 = 14 (finish limit)). LF = <b>14</b>, LS = <b>11</b>.</li><li><b>A</b> (B FS+10: LS 11-10 = 1 (finish limit)). LF = <b>1</b>, LS = <b>0</b>.</li></ul><h5>Start slack, finish slack and the completed network</h5><p>Start slack = LS − ES. Finish slack = LF − EF. An activity is critical if either is zero.</p><div class="tablewrap"><table class="calc"><thead><tr><th class="c">ID</th><th class="l"