margin:6px 8px 2px">Each box: <b>top row</b> ES | ID | EF, <b>middle row</b> start slack | activity | finish slack, <b>bottom row</b> LS | duration | LF. Red boxes and red arrows are the critical path.</p><figcaption>The completed network with early and late times</figcaption></figure><div class="final"><p class="ct">Final answer</p><p>Project duration = <b>80 days</b>.</p><p>Critical path: <b>2 → 3 → 5 → 6 → 7 → 8 → 10 → 11 → 12 → 13</b>.</p><p>Slack on the other activities: 4 = 2, 9 = 5.</p></div><h5>How sensitive is the network?</h5><p>There is <b>one critical path</b> (2 → 3 → 5 → 6 → 7 → 8 → 10 → 11 → 12 → 13). The least slack on a non-critical activity is <b>2</b> (activity 4), against a project length of 80. The network is fairly <b>sensitive</b>: a small slip on that path could make it critical too.</p><div class="diff"><b>What is different here:</b> add up all the durations and you get <b>98 days of work</b>, but the project takes only <b>80 days</b> because Fabricate parts (4) runs beside Procure parts (3). Keep both numbers: the work total (98) matters again in Part B.</div><aside class="callout exam"><p class="ct">Your professor's solution (slide 27)</p><p>Critical path 2-3-5-6-7-8-10-11-12-13, project duration 80 working days, total sum of durations 98 days. Activity 4 has 2 days of slack and activity 9 has 5. These match the table above.</p></aside></div></details>
