<h4>CyClon: converting relationships to start-to-start lags</h4>
<div class="restate"><p>Part C. Management wants the project done as soon as possible with no additional resources. The team concludes these can become start-to-start lags: Procure prototype parts 6 days after the start of Design; Fabricate parts 9 days after the start of Design; Laboratory test 1 day after the start of Assemble prototype; Field test 5 days after the start of Laboratory test; Adjust design 7 days after the start of Field test; Order stock and Order custom components 5 days after Adjust design; Test unit 9 days after the start of Assemble test production unit; Document results 3 days after the start of Test unit. Enter all nine SS lags. What impact did they have on Part A? How long will the project take? Is there a change in the critical path? In sensitivity? Why would management like this solution?</p></div>
