 class="sl" x="705.0" y="105.0" text-anchor="middle">0</text><text class="n" x="607.0" y="127.7" text-anchor="middle">59</text><text class="du" x="656.0" y="127.7" text-anchor="middle">5</text><text class="n" x="705.0" y="127.7" text-anchor="middle">64</text></g></svg><p class="mini" style="margin:6px 8px 2px">Each box: <b>top row</b> ES | ID | EF, <b>middle row</b> start slack | activity | finish slack, <b>bottom row</b> LS | duration | LF. Red boxes and red arrows are the critical path.</p><figcaption>The hypothetical project: t_e is the duration in each box</figcaption></figure>
<p>Forward and backward pass as in Chapter 6: the critical path is <b>A → B → D → F</b>, with T<sub>E</sub> = 30 + 13 + 16 + 5 = <b>64</b>. (The other path A-C-E-F = 30 + 20 + 6 + 5 = 61 is 3 shorter.)</p>
<h5 style="font:700 16px var(--sans);margin:18px 0 6px">Step 2. Uncertainty of the project</h5>
<p>Add the variances of the critical activities only: 25 + 9 + 1 + 1 = <b>36</b>. σ<sub>TE</sub> = √36 = <b>6</b>.</p>
<h5 style="font:700 16px var(--sans);margin:18px 0 6px">Step 3. Probability of finishing by 67 time units</h5>
<p>Z = (67 − 64) ÷ 6 = <b>+0.50</b>. In the table +0.4 gives 0.655 and +0.6 gives 0.726, so +0.5 gives about <b>0.69</b>.</p>
<h5 style="font:700 16px var(--sans);margin:18px 0 6px">Step 4. Probability of finishing by 60 time units</h5>
<p>Z = (60 − 64) ÷ 6 = <b>−0.67</b>. Between −0.8 (0.212) and −0.6 (0.274): about <b>0.25</b>.</p>
<div class="final"><p class="ct">Final answer</p><p>There is about a <b>69% chance</b> of finishing by 67 and about a <b>25% chance</b> of finishing by 60. The expected duration (64) is the 50% point.</p></div>

