<section id="ch7-questions" class="section-block"><h3 style="margin-top:50px">Practice questions: worked solutions</h3><p class="mini">Every question follows the same six steps. The first is taught slowly; the rest show what is new.</p><section class="qgroup"><h3>Type 1: Probability of meeting a target date</h3><p><b>How to recognise it:</b> three estimates per activity (or t<sub>e</sub> and variance) and the question 'what is the probability of completing in X?'. <b>Method:</b> t<sub>e</sub>, variance, critical path, σ, Z, table.</p><article class="q" id="c7q1" data-q="c7q1">
<header><span class="qref">Book Appendix 7.1, Exercise 1 · p. 296</span>
<label class="done"><input type="checkbox" data-done="c7q1"> I have practiced this</label></header>
<h4>National Holiday Toy: probability of 93 time units</h4>
<div class="restate"><p>Given the project information in the following table, what is the probability of completing the National Holiday Toy project in 93 time units?</p><div class="tablewrap"><table class="calc"><thead><tr><th class="c">ID</th><th class="l">Activity</th><th class="l">Predecessor</th><th class="r">Optimistic a</th><th class="r">Most likely m</th><th class="r">Pessimistic b</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="c">1</td><td class="l">Design package</td><td class="l">None</td><td class="r">6</td><td class="r">12</td><td class="r">24</td></tr><tr><td class="c">2</td><td class="l">Design product</td><td class="l">1</td><td class="r">16</td><td class="r">19</td><td class="r">28</td></tr><tr><td class="c">3</td><td class="l">Build package</td><td class="l">1</td><td class="r">4</td><td class="r">7</td><td class="r">10</td></tr><tr><td class="c">4</td><td class="l">Secure patent</td><td class="l">2</td><td class="r">24</td><td class="r">27</td><td class="r">36</td></tr><tr><td class="c">5</td><td class="l">Build product</td><td class="l">2</td><td class="r">17</td><td class="r">29</td><td class="r">47</td></tr><tr><td class="c">6</td><td class="l">Paint</td><td class="l">3, 4, 5</td><td class="r">4</td><td class="r">7</td><td class="r">10</td></tr><tr><td class="c">7</td><td class="l">Test market</td><td class="l">6</td><td class="r">13</td><td class="r">16</td><td class="r">19</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Show the solution and the teaching</summary><div class="sol">
<h5>Step 1. Recognise the type</h5>
<p>Three time estimates and the question "probability of completing in 93 time units": a <b>PERT probability</b> question. The plan:</p>
<ol class="steps"><li>Work out t<sub>e</sub> and the variance for every activity.</li><li>Use t<sub>e</sub> as the duration and find the critical path and T<sub>E</sub>.</li><li>Add the variances of the critical-path activities and take the square root.</li><li>Compute Z = (T<sub>s</sub> − T<sub>E</sub>) ÷ σ and read the probability.</li></ol>
<h5>Step 2. t<sub>e</sub> and variance for each activity</h5>
<p>Example, activity 1: t<sub>e</sub> = (6 + 4×12 + 24) ÷ 6 = 78 ÷ 6 = 13. Variance = ((24 − 6) ÷ 6)<sup>2</sup> = 3<sup>2</sup> = 9.</p>
<div class="tablewrap"><table class="calc"><thead><tr><th class="c">ID</th><th class="l">Activity</th><th class="l">Predecessor</th><th class="r">a</th><th class="r">m</th><th class="r">b</th><th class="r">t<sub>e</sub> = (a + 4m + b) ÷ 6</th><th class="r">Variance = ((b − a) ÷ 6)<sup>2</sup></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="c">1</td><td class="l">Design package</td><td class="l">None</td><td class="r">6</td><td class="r">12</td><td class="r">24</td><td class="r">13</td><td class="r">9</td></tr><tr><td class="c">2</td><td class="l">Design product</td><td class="l">1</td><td class="r">16</td><td class="r">19</td><td class="r">28</td><td class="r">20</td><td class="r">4</td></tr><tr><td class="c">3</td><td class="l">Build package</td><td class="l">1</td><td class="r">4</td><td class="r">7</td><td class="r">10</td><td class="r">7</td><td class="r">1</td></tr><tr><td class="c">4</td><td class="l">Secure patent</td><td class="l">2</td><td class="r">24</td><td class="r">27</td><td class="r">36</td><td class="r">28</td><td class="r">4</td></tr><tr><td class="c">5</td><td class="l">Build product</td><td class="l">2</td><td class="r">17</td><td class="r">29</td><td class="r">47</td><td class="r">30</td><td class="r">25</td></tr><tr><td class="c">6</td><td class="l">Paint</td><td class="l">3, 4, 5</td><td class="r">4</td><td class="r">7</td><td class="r">10</td><td class="r">7</td><td class="r">1</td></tr><tr><td class="c">7</td><td class="l">Test market</td><td class="l">6</td><td class="r">13</td><td class="r">16</td><td class="r">19</td><td class="r">16</td><td class="r">1</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
