<h5>Variance, Z and probability</h5>
<p>Variances on 1, 4, 6, 8: 3 + 2 + 10 + 1 = <b>16</b>; σ = √16 = <b>4</b>. Z = (25 − 28) ÷ 4 = <b>-0.75</b>. Table: −0.8 → 0.212, −0.6 → 0.274, so about <b>0.23</b> (exact 0.23).</p>
<div class="final"><p class="ct">Final answer</p><p>The probability of completing the project in 25 periods is about <b>0.23 (23%)</b>. It is low because the target (25) is <i>earlier</i> than the expected duration (28), so Z is negative.</p></div>
<div class="diff"><b>What is different here:</b> the target date is <b>before</b> T<sub>E</sub>, so Z is negative and the answer is below 50%. Use the symmetry rule as a check: P(−0.75) = 1 − P(+0.75) = 1 − 0.773 = 0.227.</div>
