<div class="final"><p class="ct">Final answer</p><p>The probability of finishing by day 112 is about <b>0.39</b> and by day 116 about <b>0.61</b>. The two targets are the same distance (2 days) either side of the expected 114, so the probabilities add to 1.</p></div>
<h5>Part 5. Probability of completing "Negotiate with unions" (activity 11) by day 90</h5>
<p>This asks about a <b>segment</b> of the network, not the whole project. Use only the path that leads to activity 11: <b>4 → 11</b>. Its expected finish is 26 + 60 = <b>86</b> days. The variance of that path is 4 + 100 = <b>104</b>, so σ = √104 = <b>10.20</b>.</p>
<p>Z = (90 − 86) ÷ 10.20 = <b>0.39</b>. Table: +0.2 → 0.579 and +0.4 → 0.655, so about <b>0.65</b> (exact 0.65).</p>
<div class="final"><p class="ct">Final answer</p><p>The probability that 'Negotiate with unions' is finished by day 90 is about <b>65%</b>.</p></div>
