<p>The forward pass gives an expected duration of <b>69 days</b>, which is exactly the "69 days" the case states. The critical chain is 2 → 9 → 10 → 16 → 14 → (one of the switchover meetings) → 24 → 25 → 26 → 27 → 28.</p>
<aside class="callout trap"><p class="ct">A tie in the critical path, and a mismatch with the book's tick marks</p><p>Two switchover meetings, <b>Facilities (18)</b> and <b>Systems and applications (21)</b>, both have t<sub>e</sub> = 8, so <b>two critical paths tie at 69 days</b>. The book's tick marks show Customer service (22) and Power check (23) as critical, but with these numbers they are not (22 has t<sub>e</sub> = 7). I follow the numbers. When paths tie, use the one with the <b>larger variance</b> (the more cautious choice): here that is the path through activity 21.</p></aside>
<h5>Step 3. Variance along the critical path (through 21)</h5>
<p>Common activities 2, 9, 10, 16, 14, 24, 25, 26, 27, 28: 4.83; plus activity 21: 1. Total = <b>5.83</b>, σ = <b>2.42</b> days. (Through activity 18 the total would be 4.94 and σ = 2.22, a very similar result.)</p>
<h5>Step 4. Question 1: the probability of finishing before 68 days</h5>
<p>Z = (68 − 69) ÷ 2.42 = <b>-0.41</b>. Table: −0.6 → 0.274, −0.4 → 0.345, so about <b>0.34</b> (through 18: 0.33).</p>
<h5>Step 5. Question 2: what expected duration gives a 93% chance of finishing within 68 days?</h5>
<p>A probability of 0.93 needs Z ≈ <b>1.48</b> (table: 1.4 → 0.919, 1.6 → 0.945). Solve T<sub>E</sub> = T<sub>s</sub> − Z × σ = 68 − 1.48 × 2.42 = <b>64.4 days</b>.</p>
<div class="final"><p class="ct">Final answer</p><p>(1) The chance of completing before 68 days is only about <b>34%</b>. (2) To have a 93% chance of finishing within 68 days, the expected project duration would have to fall to about <b>64 days</b> (from 69), or the estimates would have to become less uncertain.</p></div>
</div></details>
