<aside class="callout trap"><p class="ct">Common mistakes</p><ul><li>Adding variances of activities that are not on the critical path.</li><li>Adding standard deviations instead of variances.</li><li>Forgetting the square root.</li><li>Using the wrong sign for Z (target earlier than T<sub>E</sub> means negative Z and a probability below 50%).</li><li>Mixing up (b − a) ÷ 6 with the variance: the variance is the square of it.</li></ul></aside>
