<h5>Step 2. Cut every estimate to 50/50</h5>
<div class="tablewrap"><table class="calc"><thead><tr><th class="c">ID</th><th class="l">Activity</th><th class="r">Original estimate</th><th class="r">CCPM estimate (50%, odd rounded up)</th><th class="r">Safety removed</th><th class="l">Resource</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="c">P</td><td class="l">Design Sub-system A</td><td class="r">8</td><td class="r">4</td><td class="r">4</td><td class="l">Design Team A</td></tr><tr><td class="c">Q</td><td class="l">Manufacture Sub-system A</td><td class="r">12</td><td class="r">6</td><td class="r">6</td><td class="l">Technician</td></tr><tr><td class="c">R</td><td class="l">Test Sub-system A</td><td class="r">8</td><td class="r">4</td><td class="r">4</td><td class="l">Test team</td></tr><tr><td class="c">S</td><td class="l">Design Sub-system B</td><td class="r">4</td><td class="r">2</td><td class="r">2</td><td class="l">Design Team B</td></tr><tr><td class="c">T</td><td class="l">Build Sub-system B</td><td class="r">20</td><td class="r">10</td><td class="r">10</td><td class="l">Technician</td></tr><tr><td class="c">Z</td><td class="l">Assemble A and B</td><td class="r">4</td><td class="r">2</td><td class="r">2</td><td class="l">Technician</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>Critical path after cutting: 4 + 6 + 4 + 2 = <b>16 weeks</b> (P-Q-R-Z), and the B-side chain S + T = 2 + 10 = <b>12 weeks</b> feeds into Z. The safety removed from the critical chain is 32 − 16 = 16 weeks, and 24 − 12 = 12 weeks from the feeding chain (your slide draws these as the "Project Buffer, 16" and "Feeding Buffer, 12" struck through).</p>
<h5>Step 3. Size the buffers (50% rule)</h5>
<div class="tablewrap"><table class="calc"><thead><tr><th class="l">Buffer</th><th class="l">Protects</th><th class="l">Length of chain</th><th class="r">Buffer = 50%</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="l">Project buffer</td><td class="l">The end date (after Z)</td><td class="l">16 weeks (P + Q + R + Z)</td><td class="r"><b>8 weeks</b></td></tr><tr><td class="l">Feeding buffer</td><td class="l">Merge of the S-T side path into Z</td><td class="l">12 weeks (S + T)</td><td class="r"><b>6 weeks</b></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<h5>Step 4. Put the buffers into the schedule (your professor's 28 weeks)</h5>
<p>The feeding buffer sits between T and Z. Then the B-side path is S (2) + T (10) + feeding buffer (6) = <b>18 weeks</b>, which is <i>longer</i> than P + Q + R = 14 weeks. So Z can only start at week 18, not week 14. Z takes 2 more weeks (finishing at week 20), and the project buffer adds 8: <b>20 + 8 = 28 weeks</b>.</p>
