<div class="final"><p class="ct">Final answer</p><p>With 50% estimates and buffers, the plan is <b>28 weeks</b> (down from 32). The chain S-T-Feeding buffer-Z-Project buffer is now the longest path, so P, Q and R have 4 weeks of slack.</p></div>
<h5>Step 5. The resource conflict: the Technician is needed for both Q and T</h5>
<p>Q, T and Z all need the same Technician (the pink boxes on your slide). T (10 weeks) runs in weeks 2 to 12, so the Technician is <b>not free to start Q until week 12</b>, even though P is finished at week 4. That creates a <b>resource dependency</b> T → Q, so the <b>critical chain is now S → T → Q → R → Z</b>, not P → Q → R → Z. Its length is 2 + 10 + 6 + 4 + 2 = <b>24 weeks</b>. P becomes the side path (a feeder into Q) with a feeding buffer, drawn as 4 weeks on your slide.</p>
