<aside class="callout trap"><p class="ct">Check the slide's numbers against this</p><p>Your slide shows the feeding buffer in front of Q as 4 weeks. By the 50% rule a feeding chain of only P (4 weeks) would need a buffer of 2; the slide draws 4. It does not change the schedule (P + buffer = 8 weeks is still shorter than the 12 weeks T needs), so the chain and the 24 weeks are unaffected. If the exam gives its own buffer size, use that.</p></aside>
