<h4>Print Software project with critical-chain scheduling</h4>
<div class="restate"><p>Apply critical-chain scheduling principles to the Print Software, Inc., project (Exercise 10 in Chapter 6). Revise the estimated time durations by 50 percent, except round up the odd time durations (for example, 3 becomes 4 before halving, so 2). Draw a CCPM network diagram similar to Figure A8.3 for the Print Software project, as well as a Gantt chart similar to Figure A8.4. How would these diagrams differ from the ones generated using the traditional scheduling technique?</p><div class="tablewrap"><table class="calc"><thead><tr><th class="c">ID</th><th class="l">Description</th><th class="l">Predecessor(s)</th><th class="r">Time (days)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="c">A</td><td class="l">External specifications</td><td class="l">None</td><td class="r">8</td></tr><tr><td class="c">B</td><td class="l">Review design features</td><td class="l">A</td><td class="r">2</td></tr><tr><td class="c">C</td><td class="l">Document new features</td><td class="l">A</td><td class="r">3</td></tr><tr><td class="c">D</td><td class="l">Write software</td><td class="l">A</td><td class="r">60</td></tr><tr><td class="c">E</td><td class="l">Program and test</td><td class="l">B</td><td class="r">40</td></tr><tr><td class="c">F</td><td class="l">Edit and publish notes</td><td class="l">C</td><td class="r">2</td></tr><tr><td class="c">G</td><td class="l">Review manual</td><td class="l">D</td><td class="r">2</td></tr><tr><td class="c">H</td><td class="l">Alpha site</td><td class="l">E, F</td><td class="r">20</td></tr><tr><td class="c">I</td><td class="l">Print manual</td><td class="l">G</td><td class="r">10</td></tr><tr><td class="c">J</td><td class="l">Beta site</td><td class="l">H, I</td><td class="r">10</td></tr><tr><td class="c">K</td><td class="l">Manufacture</td><td class="l">J</td><td class="r">12</td></tr><tr><td class="c">L</td><td class="l">Release and ship</td><td class="l">K</td><td class="r">3</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Show the solution and the teaching</summary><div class="sol">
<h5>Step 1. Recognise the type</h5>
<p>"Apply critical-chain scheduling principles" with "revise durations by 50 percent". So: (1) halve every duration (odd ones rounded up: 3 becomes 2), (2) find the critical chain, (3) size the project and feeder buffers, (4) draw the network with buffers and a Gantt chart, (5) compare with the traditional schedule.</p>
<h5>Step 2. Halve the durations</h5>
<div class="tablewrap"><table class="calc"><thead><tr><th class="c">ID</th><th class="l">Activity</th><th class="r">Original estimate</th><th class="r">CCPM estimate (50%, odd rounded up)</th><th class="r">Safety removed</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="c">A</td><td class="l">External specifications</td><td class="r">8</td><td class="r">4</td><td class="r">4</td></tr><tr><td class="c">B</td><td class="l">Review design features</td><td class="r">2</td><td class="r">1</td><td class="r">1</td></tr><tr><td class="c">C</td><td class="l">Document new features</td><td class="r">3</td><td class="r">2</td><td class="r">1</td></tr><tr><td class="c">D</td><td class="l">Write software</td><td class="r">60</td><td class="r">30</td><td class="r">30</td></tr><tr><td class="c">E</td><td class="l">Program and test</td><td class="r">40</td><td class="r">20</td><td class="r">20</td></tr><tr><td class="c">F</td><td class="l">Edit and publish notes</td><td class="r">2</td><td class="r">1</td><td class="r">1</td></tr><tr><td class="c">G</td><td class="l">Review manual</td><td class="r">2</td><td class="r">1</td><td class="r">1</td></tr><tr><td class="c">H</td><td class="l">Alpha site</td><td class="r">20</td><td class="r">10</td><td class="r">10</td></tr><tr><td class="c">I</td><td class="l">Print manual</td><td class="r">10</td><td class="r">5</td><td class="r">5</td></tr><tr><td class="c">J</td><td class="l">Beta site</td><td class="r">10</td><td class="r">5</td><td class="r">5</td></tr><tr><td class="c">K</td><td class="l">Manufacture</td><td class="r">12</td><td class="r">6</td><td class="r">6</td></tr><tr><td class="c">L</td><td class="l">Release and ship</td><td class="r">3</td><td class="r">2</td><td class="r">1</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<h5>Step 3. Critical chain</h5>
<p>The Print Software exercise gives no resource information, so the critical chain is simply the critical path of the halved network: <b>A → D → G → I → J → K → L</b> = 4 + 30 + 1 + 5 + 5 + 6 + 2 = <b>53 days</b> (the traditional plan was 105 days). The activities B, C, E, F and H are off the chain.</p>
<h5>Step 4. Buffers</h5>
<div class="tablewrap"><table class="calc"><thead><tr><th class="l">Buffer</th><th class="l">Where</th><th class="l">Chain length</th><th class="r">50% (rounded up)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="l">Project buffer</td><td class="l">After L, at the end of the critical chain</td><td class="l">53 days</td><td class="r"><b>27 days</b></td></tr><tr><td class="l">Feeder buffer</td><td class="l">Where the side path B → E → H joins the critical chain at J (Beta site)</td><td class="l">31 days (B 1 + E 20 + H 10)</td><td class="r"><b>16 days</b></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p class="mini">C and F (3 days after halving) feed H, which is itself off the chain, so the feeder buffer on the B-E-H chain covers them; the book only places feeder buffers where a non-critical path merges into the critical chain.</p>
<h5>Step 5. The CCPM network and schedule</h5>
<p>Add the feeder buffer between H and J and the project buffer after L, then do the forward pass. The side path B-E-H (31 days) plus its 16-day buffer is <b>47 days</b> after A, but the critical chain reaches J after only D + G + I = 36 days, so the space available (36 days between A and J) is too small for the side path and its buffer. Beta site (J) can start only after the buffer, which pushes the end date out.</p>
