<p>The critical path is <b>A → D → F → G = 25</b>. Total normal direct cost = 50 + 80 + 60 + 50 + 100 + 40 + 70 = <b>$450</b>.</p>
<h5 style="font:700 16px var(--sans);margin:18px 0 6px">Step 2. The moves</h5>
<ul><li><b>Move 1 (25 → 24).</b> Critical path: ADFG (25). Activities on it that can still be shortened: A ($20), D ($25), F ($30). Cheapest choice: <b>A</b> at <b>$20</b> (next best: D at $25). Direct cost becomes $470.</li><li><b>Move 2 (24 → 23).</b> Critical path: ADFG (24). Activities on it that can still be shortened: D ($25), F ($30). Cheapest choice: <b>D</b> at <b>$25</b> (next best: F at $30). Direct cost becomes $495.</li><li><b>Move 3 (23 → 22).</b> Critical paths: ACFG and ADFG (23). Activities on them that can still be shortened: C ($30), D ($25), F ($30). Every critical path must be shortened, so we need the cheapest set of activities that touches <i>all</i> of them. Cheapest choice: <b>F</b> at <b>$30</b> (next best: C+D at $55). Direct cost becomes $525.</li><li><b>Move 4 (22 → 21).</b> Critical paths: ABEG and ACFG and ADFG (22). Activities on them that can still be shortened: B ($40), C ($30), D ($25), E ($30). Every critical path must be shortened, so we need the cheapest set of activities that touches <i>all</i> of them. Cheapest choice: <b>C+D+E</b> at <b>$85</b> (next best: B+C+D at $95). Direct cost becomes $610.</li></ul>
<p>Look at Move 3 to Move 4: after crashing F, all three paths (A-B-E-G, A-C-F-G and A-D-F-G) are 22 long, so the next unit must be taken from <b>all three at once</b>: C ($30) on A-C-F-G, D ($25) on A-D-F-G and E ($30) on A-B-E-G, together $85. A and F are already fully crashed, which is why they cannot help.</p>
