> Critical path: ABDGH (13). Activities on it that can still be shortened: A ($100). Cheapest choice: <b>A</b> at <b>$100</b>. Direct cost becomes $1,640.</li></ul><p><b>Stop:</b> after the last move every critical path consists only of activities that are already at their crash time (or have zero crash allowed), so the project cannot be shortened further. This is the <b>crash point</b>: <b>12</b> with direct cost <b>$1,640</b>.</p><h5>Summary of costs</h5><div class="tablewrap"><table class="calc"><thead><tr><th class="r">Project duration</th><th class="l">Activities crashed</th><th class="r">Cost of the move</th><th class="r">Total direct cost</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="r">16</td><td class="l">normal</td><td class="r"></td><td class="r">$1,400</td></tr><tr><td class="r">15</td><td class="l">G</td><td class="r">$20</td><td class="r">$1,420</td></tr><tr><td class="r">14</td><td class="l">D</td><td class="r">$40</td><td class="r">$1,460</td></tr><tr><td class="r">13</td><td class="l">B</td><td class="r">$80</td><td class="r">$1,540</td></tr><tr><td class="r">12</td><td class="l">A</td><td class="r">$100</td><td class="r">$1,640</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="final"><p class="ct">Final answer</p><p>The project is crashed from 16 to its crash point of <b>12</b>; total direct cost rises from $1,400 to <b>$1,640</b>. The moves, in order: 15: G ($20); 14: D ($40); 13: B ($80); 12: A ($100).</p></div><div class="diff"><b>What is different here:</b> only <b>one</b> path (A-B-D-G-H, 16) is long; the other two paths (11 and 8) are far shorter, so throughout the exercise there is only one critical path and every move is a single activity. Notice that C and F, though cheap-looking, are never crashed: they are on a non-critical path.</div></div></details>
