ass="ln s1" x1="203.2" x2="225.2" y1="34" y2="34"/><text class="leg" x="231.2" y="38">Indirect cost</text><line class="ln s2" x1="336.8" x2="358.8" y1="34" y2="34"/><text class="leg" x="364.8" y="38">Total project cost</text></svg><figcaption>Direct, indirect and total cost by project duration</figcaption></figure><div class="final"><p class="ct">Final answer</p><p>Crash point: <b>11</b> at direct cost $1,160. <b>Optimum cost-time schedule: 14, with total project cost $810.</b> The normal schedule costs $820, so crashing saves $10.</p></div><div class="diff"><b>What is different here:</b> this is the first question with indirect costs, so after the direct costs you add the indirect cost for each duration and pick the <b>lowest total</b>. Notice Move 3: <b>three</b> paths are critical at 13, and the cheapest way to cut all three is B + F + G = $190 (I alone would cost $200). Also B and E tie at $60 on the same path; B is chosen because it is earlier.</div></div></details>
