e="margin:6px 8px 2px">Each box: <b>top row</b> ES | ID | EF, <b>middle row</b> start slack | activity | finish slack, <b>bottom row</b> LS | duration | LF. Red boxes and red arrows are the critical path.</p><figcaption>The normal network (critical path in red); the numbers in the boxes are normal times</figcaption></figure><p>The normal project duration is <b>17</b> and the normal total direct cost is <b>$2,000</b> (the sum of the normal costs).</p><h5>The crashing moves</h5><ul><li><b>Move 1 (17 → 16).</b> Critical path: ABDHI (17). Activities on it that can still be shortened: B ($100), D ($40), H ($60), I ($200). Cheapest choice: <b>D</b> at <b>$40</b> (next best: H at $60). Direct cost becomes $2,040.</li><li><b>Move 2 (16 → 15).</b> Critical path: ABDHI (16). Activities on it that can still be shortened: B ($100), H ($60), I ($200). Cheapest choice: <b>H</b> at <b>$60</b> (next best: B at $100). Direct cost becomes $2,100.</li><li><b>Move 3 (15 → 14).</b> Critical path: ABDHI (15). Activities on it that can still be shortened: B ($100), H ($60), I ($200). Cheapest choice: <b>H</b> at <b>$60</b> (next best: B at $100). Direct cost becomes $2,160.</li><li><b>Move 4 (14 → 13).</b> Critical paths: ABDHI and ABFGI (14). Activities on them that can still be shortened: B ($100), F ($30), G ($20), I ($200). Every critical path must be shortened, so we need the cheapest set of activities that touches <i>all</i> of them. Cheapest choice: <b>B</b> at <b>$100</b> (next best: I at $200). Direct cost becomes $2,260.</li><li><b>Move 5 (13 → 12).</b> Critical paths: ABDHI and ABFGI and ACDHI (13). Activities on them that can still be shortened: C ($60), F ($30), G ($20), I ($200). Every critical path must be shortened, so we need the cheapest set of activities that touches <i>all</i> of them. Cheapest choice: <b>I</b> at <b>$200</b>. Direct cost becomes $2,460.</li></ul><p><b>Stop:</b> after the last move every critical path consists only of activities that are already at their crash time (or have zero crash allowed), so the project cannot be shortened further. This is the <b>crash point</b>: <b>12</b> with direct cost <b>$2,460</b>.</p><h5>Summary of costs</h5><p>Indirect costs are listed for each duration, from $1,500 at 17 weeks down to $1,150 at 10 weeks.</p><div class="tablewrap"><table class="calc"><thead><tr><th class="r">Project duration</th><th class="l">Activities crashed</th><th class="r">Cost of the move</th><th class="r">Total direct cost</th><th class="r">Indirect cost</th><th class="r">Total project cost</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="r">17</td><td class="l">normal</td><td class="r"></td><td class="r">$2,000</td><td class="r">$1,500</td><td class="r">$3,500</td></tr><tr class="hl"><td class="r">16</td><td class="l">D</td><td class="r">$40</td><td class="r">$2,040</td><td class="r">$1,450</td><td class="r">$3,490</td></tr><tr><td class="r">15</td><td class="l">H</td><td class="r">$60</td><td class="r">$2,100</td><td class="r">$1,400</td><td class="r">$3,500</td></tr><tr><td class="r">14</td><td class="l">H</td><td class="r">$60</td><td class="r">$2,160</td><td class="r">$1,350</td><td class="r">$3,510</td></tr><tr><td class="r">13</td><td class="l">B</td><td class="r">$100</td><td class="r">$2,260</td><td class="r">$1,300</td><td class="r">$3,560</td></tr><tr><td class="r">12</td><td class="l">I</td><td class="r">$200</td><td class="r">$2,460</td><td class="r">$1,250</td><td class="r">$3,710</td></tr></tbody></table></div><figure class="fig"><svg class="chart" viewBox="0 0 680 340" role="img" aria-label="Direct, indirect and total cost by project duration" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><line class="grid" x1="74" x2="660" y1="288.0" y2="288.0"/><text class="tick" x="66" y="292.0" text-anchor="end">0</text><line class="grid" x1="74" x2="660" y1="222.6" y2="222.6"/><text class="tick" x="66" y="226.6" text-anchor="end">1,000</text><line class="grid" x1="74" x2="660" y1="157.2" y2="157.2"/><text class="tick" x="66"