 r="3.6"/><circle class="pt s1" cx="74.0" cy="206.3" r="3.6"/><path class="ln s2" d="M660.0 59.1 L542.8 59.8 L425.6 59.1 L308.4 58.5 L191.2 55.2 L74.0 45.4"/><circle class="pt s2" cx="660.0" cy="59.1" r="3.6"/><circle class="pt s2" cx="542.8" cy="59.8" r="3.6"/><circle class="pt s2" cx="425.6" cy="59.1" r="3.6"/><circle class="pt s2" cx="308.4" cy="58.5" r="3.6"/><circle class="pt s2" cx="191.2" cy="55.2" r="3.6"/><circle class="pt s2" cx="74.0" cy="45.4" r="3.6"/><circle class="mk" cx="542.8" cy="59.8" r="6"/><text class="mkl" x="552.8" y="47.8" text-anchor="start">Optimum 16: $3,490</text><line class="ln s0" x1="84" x2="106" y1="34" y2="34"/><text class="leg" x="112" y="38">Direct cost</text><line class="ln s1" x1="203.2" x2="225.2" y1="34" y2="34"/><text class="leg" x="231.2" y="38">Indirect cost</text><line class="ln s2" x1="336.8" x2="358.8" y1="34" y2="34"/><text class="leg" x="364.8" y="38">Total project cost</text></svg><figcaption>Direct, indirect and total cost by project duration</figcaption></figure><div class="final"><p class="ct">Final answer</p><p>Crash point: <b>12</b> at direct cost $2,460. <b>Optimum cost-time schedule: 16, with total project cost $3,490.</b> The normal schedule costs $3,500, so crashing saves $10.</p></div><div class="diff"><b>What is different here:</b> each week saved is worth only <b>$50</b> of indirect cost (the list falls $50 per week). Only <b>D at $40</b> is cheaper than $50, so only Move 1 pays: the total falls from $3,500 (17 weeks) to <b>$3,490 (16 weeks)</b>. Move 2 (H at $60) costs more than the $50 it saves, so the total returns to $3,500 at 15 weeks, then keeps rising. The optimum is therefore 16 weeks. Ties: in Move 2 and Move 3 the activity H is used twice (its allowance is 2 weeks) because it is on every critical path at that point and cheaper than B ($100) or I ($200).</div></div></details>
</article></section><section class="qgroup"><h3>Type 3: A bonus, a penalty or overhead per day</h3><p>An outside payment per day changes how much a day of crashing is worth. Add it to the indirect saving when deciding whether to crash.</p><article class="q" id="c9q6" data-q="c9q6">
