<h4>Monthly status report: compute the indexes and the forecast</h4>
<div class="restate"><p>Project 163, status as of April 1, 2007. PV 588,240; EV 566,064; AC 596,800; BAC 1,051,200. Compute SV, CV, SPI, CPI, PCIB, EAC<sub>f</sub>, VAC<sub>f</sub> and TCPI, and interpret them.</p></div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Show the solution and the teaching</summary><div class="sol">
<h5>Step 1. Variances and indexes</h5>
<div class="tablewrap"><table class="calc"><thead><tr><th class="l">Measure</th><th class="l">Working</th><th class="r">Result</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="l">SV = EV − PV</td><td class="l">566,064 − 588,240</td><td class="r"><b>−22,176</b></td></tr><tr><td class="l">CV = EV − AC</td><td class="l">566,064 − 596,800</td><td class="r"><b>−30,736</b></td></tr><tr><td class="l">SPI = EV ÷ PV</td><td class="l">566,064 ÷ 588,240</td><td class="r">0.962</td></tr><tr><td class="l">CPI = EV ÷ AC</td><td class="l">566,064 ÷ 596,800</td><td class="r"><b>0.95</b></td></tr><tr><td class="l">PCIB = EV ÷ BAC</td><td class="l">566,064 ÷ 1,051,200</td><td class="r"><b>0.538</b></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<h5>Step 2. Forecast</h5>
<p>Using CPI rounded to 0.95 as the slide does: ETC = (BAC − EV) ÷ CPI = (1,051,200 − 566,064) ÷ 0.95 = 510,669. EAC<sub>f</sub> = AC + ETC = 596,800 + 510,669 = <b>1,107,469</b>. VAC<sub>f</sub> = BAC − EAC<sub>f</sub> = <b>−56,269</b>. PCIC = AC ÷ EAC = 596,800 ÷ 1,090,640 = <b>0.547</b> (using the revised estimate of 1,090,640 given on the slide).</p>
<p>TCPI = (BAC − EV) ÷ (BAC − AC) = 485,136 ÷ 454,400 = <b>1.07</b>.</p>
<div class="final"><p class="ct">Final answer</p><p>SV = −22,176, CV = −30,736, CPI = 0.95, PCIB = 0.538, EAC<sub>f</sub> = 1,107,469, VAC<sub>f</sub> = −56,269, TCPI = 1.07. The project is slightly behind schedule (about 25 days, per the slide) and over budget; to finish on budget each remaining dollar must earn about $1.07 of value, which is tough but not impossible.</p></div>
<aside class="callout exam"><p class="ct">This is your slide 37 (Monthly Status Report, project 163)</p><p>The slide shows PV 588,240; EV 566,064; AC 596,800; SV −22,176; CV −30,736; BAC 1,051,200; EAC (revised) 1,090,640; VAC −39,440; EAC<sub>f</sub> 1,107,469; CPI .95; PCIB .538; PCIC .547. Every number above reproduces it. The report also shows how a manager explains the variance in words: the schedule slipped because a design team was lost, and the cost variance is largely due to a design change.</p></aside>
</div></details>
